comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T04:25:59.589Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: a fresh complete strict all-status corpus and explicit version searches found historical refreshes plus the open coordination parent; no item covers these exact mature tooling versions."
  "2026-10-26T04:33:33.920Z","harness:codex","Exact public upstream evidence at October26 04:20 UTC: Knip6.42.0 published October18 13:44:32.638Z; CodeQL action4.39.0 October15 10:57:05Z; CodSpeed action5.5.0 October14 11:38:37Z. All exceed seven full days and official action tag refs match the adopted immutable SHAs. TruffleHog3.99.3 was published October19 18:21:40Z and is not eligible until October26 18:21:40Z; both existing3.99.2 action/binary pins remain untouched. Frozen-lock install passed. Current full static, linked contracts and exact-head hosted acceptance follow before closure."
  "2026-10-26T05:07:09.986Z","harness:codex","The linked workflow suite correctly detected its old exact CodSpeed action SHA after adoption: 32 tests passed and the existing immutable-pin assertion failed. Update that one expected SHA to the independently verified v5.5.0 tag; retain Ubuntu22.04, Node24, simulation mode, no stale instrument caches, all permission checks and every deadline unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T05:21:07.255Z","harness:codex","PR1596 final tooling validation: all33 existing workflow/dependency contract tests pass after updating the exact CodSpeed SHA assertion. Frozen lockfile installation, source static dependency/advisory/cooldown checks, runtime42-package lock, workflow permission checks and build pass. Merge of prepared release2026.10.26 changed distribution versions only. Dependabot1599/1601 will be closed with this canonical PM link after the combined delivery lands; the immature TruffleHog update remains deferred under the existing coordinator."
  "2026-10-26T14:48:07.955Z","harness:codex","Latest-package verification: npm published pm-changelog 2026.10.26 during this delivery. Updated the managed project package through pm package install and generated/checked CHANGELOG.md with version 2026.10.26. Fresh isolated npm and Bun installations of published pm-cli 2026.10.26 both install and activate this extension, pass deep package diagnostics and contracts, and execute changelog upgrades for api-user, operator and agent-behavior with complete no-obligation results for the 2026.10.25 to 2026.10.26 range. Their npx and bunx launchers report 2026.10.26. The initial probe used an output-budget flag unsupported on that extension surface in the published host; the structured refusal is retained, and the supported command invocation passes. No pm-changelog source fix or host workaround is needed."
  "2026-10-26T16:47:10.328Z","harness:codex","Hosted CI40351508407 static gate correctly refused new changelog upgrades: missing destination and undeclared positional signature. Latest pm-changelog 2026.10.26 is functional; the host census was stale. The existing published-package contract table now includes upgrades with no positionals and fails before the SDK census fix: 18 focused cases pass and the one new table row fails. Add the package-owned destination, retaining package ownership, grammar budgets and every gate."
  "2026-10-26T17:52:09.936Z","harness:codex","CI remediation validation: the existing package contract table fails on its new upgrades row against the old SDK census and passes after the package-owned destination is added. The generated full contract fixture adds twelve lines for destination and empty positional metadata; public SDK type surface has zero classified changes. All linked commands and 23 focused cases pass. Complete source coverage passes 11,461 tests with three platform skips and exact 100/100/100/100: 71,030 statements, 54,658 branches, 14,612 functions and 67,194 lines covered, with unchanged denominators. Functional static, dependency/advisory/cooldown, SDK/MCP/schema, graph/record and mutation stages pass; current SDK import admission passes. Qualified local CLI transport failures also occur on immutable main and remain retained with the startup investigation owner. No monolithic local static success is claimed; fresh exact-head hosted static is required."
  "2026-10-26T18:19:18.854Z","harness:codex","TypeScript ESLint 8.72.0 published October 19 at 17:08:09.147 UTC and exceeded seven full days before this update. All eleven new lockfile entries are the matching 8.72.0 family and their individual publication timestamps pass the same age check. An extra command-local blanket pnpm age setting initially refused pre-existing fast-uri 3.1.9, the completed independent-feed security floor. That setting is not repository policy; ordinary repository defaults install the mature tooling while preserving the existing security override. No exclusion, override, updater cooldown or committed policy is relaxed. The original refusal is retained."
  "2026-10-26T18:35:02.141Z","harness:codex","Exact adoption evidence: TypeScript ESLint 8.72.0 was published October 19 at 17:08:09.147 UTC; Knip 6.42.1 at 18:24:59.186 UTC; TruffleHog 3.99.3 at 18:21:40 UTC. Each update was performed only after its seven-day cutoff. All twelve new lock entries have individually verified publication evidence; no unrelated transitive upgrade is introduced. TruffleHog action commit e63326d6545de8f425d93ce24078c6e68d83f70e matches the official v3.99.3 tag, and its explicit binary version is 3.99.3. Existing scanner options, exclusions, verification requirements and read-only workflow permissions remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T18:35:02.824Z","harness:codex","New tooling verification passes: frozen lockfile install, registry and independent-feed dependency gates, Knip export analysis with its native negative control, all workflow/dependency contract cases, updater cooldown, workflow permissions and the 42-package runtime lock. ESLint and TypeScript both pass with TypeScript ESLint 8.72.0. Current CodSpeed job initially failed only while downloading installer 5.5.0 with HTTP 504; the single native rerun passed. No action-source workaround or provider/threshold change was needed. Full review of source head 98b71c355 completed without unresolved findings; the upcoming dependency head still requires fresh checks and review."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T17:52:12.442Z","harness:codex","Activating a new package version and exercising its command is not a complete host integration check. Synchronize the SDK destination/positional census and generated contract fixture when the package adds a command, then execute the actual grammar and static gates."
